    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class (the other two files are the base class and a helper). The full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the GOLD membership tier rule: `membershipTier` is now `'GOLD'` when the owner's household (owners sharing the same `householdId`) has 3 or more members after the create; otherwise the existing SILVER/BRONZE rules apply.\n\nFollowing the existing `namesakeCount` pattern (a value computed in the controller and read by the mapper), the changes were:\n\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `@Transient Integer householdMemberCount` field with getter/setter. It's transient because household size is a derived, point-in-time value, not persisted state.\n\n- **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 `membershipTier(Owner)` now returns `\"GOLD\"` first when `householdMemberCount >= 3`, then falls back to the unchanged SILVER/BRONZE logic.\n\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 added a `countHouseholdMembers(householdId)` helper (counts owners sharing a non-null `householdId`, `0` for no household), and populate `householdMemberCount` on the owner both right after create (`addOwner`, after the save so the new member is counted) and on read (`getOwner`, before mapping). Computing it live at read time means the tier stays correct as a household grows, which is what the test exercises: it reads the third member back via `GET` and expects GOLD.\n\n`./mvnw test` \u2192 BUILD SUCCESS, `AcceptanceTest.coreGoldForThreeMemberHousehold` passing (1 test, 0 failures).",
